    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\delta_{i} = 1 $ when the difference within parentheses is positive and $ \\delta_{i} = 0 $ otherwise. To test for the significance of cross-over interaction between the two genotypic groups, the minimum of the two statistics is compared with critical values given in Table 1 of Gail and Simon (1985). Large values of the final test statistic imply that cross-overs occur more frequently than can be expected by chance, given the observed sampling variances of the means.",
